<?php

/*
| The Odoo archive (docs/odoo/WAVE2.md §3): what each model of the copy of Odoo IS for a person.
|
| The copy (`odoo_records`) keeps every record as Odoo returned it. This file says how a record becomes a row of the
| index `odoo_docs` (its number, title, partner, date, state, amount, what it hangs on) and how it is shown: the
| columns of its list, its filters, the summary of its page, its lines and its related documents. Nothing here is
| code: App\Integration\Odoo\Archive reads it. After changing how a kind is INDEXED (the keys number … search below),
| run `php artisan scm:odoo-archive-index`: the models whose definitions changed are indexed again by themselves.
|
| A KIND
|   model, section, label [ar, en], one [ar, en] (one document of it)
|   when        conditions on the record that make it this kind: field => [values]; null = empty. The kinds of a model
|               are tried in the order of this file; one without `when` takes the rest.
|   view        [kind, dim1|dim2 => value]: no rows of its own — a named, filtered list of another kind.
|   number, title, partner, product, date, state, amount, residual, currency, user, dim1, dim2, seq
|               where the typed columns of the index come from (a VALUE, below). `dateType` says whether `date` is a
|               day ('date') or a moment ('datetime', the default). A dimension that people filter by is written
|               [value, [ar, en], 'choices' => set | 'model' => Odoo model | 'text' => true].
|   parent      what the record hangs on: [field => Odoo model, …] (the first one that has a value), or
|               ['@ref' => [model field, id field]] for Odoo's "any document" pairs. Lines hang on their order,
|               a credit note on its invoice, a delivery on its sales order: that is how a page finds its lines and
|               its follow-up documents.
|   search      more fields the search box matches (number, title and partner name always are).
|   via         [many2one field => Odoo model]: the record that field points at is read too; its values are
|               written `field>name`.
|   touch       [field => Odoo model]: records to index again when this one changes (they show values of it).
|   states      the choices of `state`: a set of `choices` below, or value => [ar, en, tone];
|               `stateModel`: the state is a stage (a many2one) of that model.
|   columns     the list. A column is 'number' | 'title' | 'partner' | 'product' | 'date' | 'state' | 'amount' | 'user'
|               (the typed columns, labelled by `labels`), or [key, type, [ar, en], from?, 'choices' => set].
|               `from` is a VALUE; '#dim1', '#dim2', '#residual' read the index. Types: text, number, qty, money,
|               date, datetime, state, partner, product, user, bool.
|   inline      the columns shown when its rows are the lines of another document (default: columns).
|   summary     the head of its page: columns again.
|   sections    its lines: [kind, [ar, en], 'groups' => [...]] — the rows of that kind that hang on it.
|   related     documents it points at ('ids' => field, 'model' => …), documents that name it
|               ('kinds' => [...], 'dim2' => '#number'), what settled it ('reconciled' => true). Everything that
|               hangs on it through `parent` is listed without being named here.
|   line        its rows are lines of a document: not part of the search across kinds.
|   support     indexed for the pages of other documents only (messages, value changes): never listed.
|   hangs       it hangs on any document ('@ref'): a row is people's file when that document is.
|   private     people's file whatever the model. `personal` => a pattern of field names shown only with odoo.private.
|
| A VALUE is a field name; `a|b` the first that has a value; `m2o>name` a value of the record `m2o` points at (see
| via); `@display` Odoo's display name; `@id` the record's id; `flag:f` '1' when f is set or positive, else '0';
| `code:f` the first word of f (the code of "201002 Payables"); `id:f` the id of a many2one; `tmpl:f` the product
| behind a product template; `@company` (as a currency) the currency of the record's company.
|
| Who may read: page.odoo. A kind built on people's files (App\Integration\Odoo\OdooSync::isRestricted) also needs
| odoo.private. Tones are the chip colours of the client: ok, warn, bad, blue, violet, neutral, off.
*/

